        "node_id": "n_13_d85abe",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous reasoning was that it assumed the GCD of all monster healths would be the minimum possible final health. However, this is not always the case. The minimum possible final health is the GCD of all monster healths, but the process of attacking and reducing healths can lead to a smaller final health. The key insight is that the minimum possible final health is the GCD of all monster healths, but we need to consider the cumulative effect of all attacks on each monster.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-160947873808500017",
